<%# The original, recovered 2026-08-13 from the CodePen export kept whole at
    RAILS/shared/reference/banner_art/. This file's placeholder asked for "the
    exact snippet ... when ready" and carried a stand-in until then: 18 filled
    hearts blended with mix-blend-mode: screen.

    This is that snippet, with one deviation. The original grids at 50vmin,
    which was right for a 300x300 banner and under-fills .dating-heart-stage
    (min(92vw, 520px) x min(58vh, 480px)); the doodle is sized 100% by
    _vertical_dating_intro.scss, so the grid follows the stage instead.

    frame: is what makes it read — the hearts are outlines, not fills, and each
    one is filled by its own rotating gradient stripe via :after. The glow is
    two drop-shadows rather than a box-shadow, so it is not what the flat-UI
    rule forbids. css-doodle is self-hosted at /vendor/css-doodle.min.js and
    loaded by dating/home/index.html.erb; nothing here reaches a CDN. %>
<div class="dating-heart-stage" aria-hidden="true">
  <css-doodle class="dating-heart-doodle">
    :doodle {
      @grid: 1x10 / 100% 100%;
      filter:
        drop-shadow(0 0 10px #ff360e) drop-shadow(0 0 20px #ff360e);
    }

    @size: calc(100% - @i * 3%);
    @place-cell: center;

    clip-path: @shape(
      points: 180;
      a: cos(t)*13/18 - cos(2t)*5/18;
      b: cos(3t)/18 + cos(4t)/18;
      x: .75 * sin(t)^3;
      y: a - b + .15;
      frame: @r(2, 2.5);
    );

    :after {
      content: '';
      @place-cell: center;
      @size: @p(@r(10px), @m5(@r(50%))) 100%;
      background: linear-gradient(@r(360deg),
        #30182b, #f0f1bc, #60f0c0, #ff360e, #191f04);
      animation: cycle @r(2s, 8s) linear infinite;
      animation-delay: -@r(8s);
    }

    @keyframes cycle {
      to {
        transform: rotate(1turn);
      }
    }
  </css-doodle>
</div>
